{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792798376,"nonce":"BqFQ5kpSRKblttaLSaOOjUiERCs=","message":"Implemented in af0870910e77d3293d51ce6f3e864edcfe0a730f.\n\nThe local slice provides explicit Share/Join/Copy Invitation/Leave commands, a status menu, one shared text document, exact UTF-16 editor transactions, Yrs author undo/redo, remote carets/selections/names, composition deferral, inactive-view synchronization, state-vector reconnect and explicit room shutdown. Networking runs on a native worker; unused Jam starts no worker or polling. Queues have count and byte limits, native handles close explicitly, and slow-send cancellation releases its byte budget. Invitations use OS-generated secrets and numeric loopback addresses; another machine uses SSH forwarding. Renames/deletes require leaving the shared document.\n\nAshui hooks are committed as 3f1d69ab445177cf45d94fdddb51750908ab328a on the isolated jam-editor-hooks branch, tracked in its issue 523c5bdc7e24961a7491498b5ed94b0a77f77eb640124eacdd2b8a0ccf23146e. RayDE pins the commit. Unrelated dirty sibling changes were preserved.\n\nValidation: seven native tests passed (concurrent/reordered/duplicate Unicode updates, per-author undo/redo, invalid edits, actual WebSocket sync/presence/reconnect/closure, version/token rejection, malformed updates and slow-send byte ownership). Clippy with all targets and warnings denied passed. Standalone Ashui CodeCollaboration and RayDE JamWorkbenchChecks passed; the latter ran in hybrid and AOT modes, light and dark themes. Existing code-action UI/undo regression checks passed in both themes. The native peer driver also passed between macOS and the Linux NUC through an SSH reverse loopback tunnel while the NUC was available; Linux native tests passed there. This was a native-client interoperability run, not a Linux GUI run. Final native/local and AOT editor checks were repeated after the bounded queue and invitation changes.\n\nBuilt bin/rayde.hl, bin/rayde and bin/RayDE.app. The bundle has the final native library (matching the staged library SHA-256) and passed deep/strict signature verification. Source and dependency notices are included. Reproduce with bash scripts/check-jam.sh; the cross-machine driver requires an available remote host and prebuilt client.\n\nScope: one document, 1 MiB text, up to eight peers, ephemeral room state and in-memory acknowledgements. Local files change only on Save. Hosted durable storage/checkpoints, accounts/roles/billing, browser integration, assets, follow mode, providers, OBS and media remain in their roadmap issues. No RSS/idle-CPU performance claim is inferred from the ownership tests.","files":null}]}